# AI Feature Rules

AI accelerates the product but is never the source of truth.

## AI may

- Explain findings and requirements in developer language
- Locate relevant code and likely root causes
- Propose remediations and generate candidate code/config changes
- Generate tests and summarize evidence

## AI must never

- Set or change a requirement/finding status directly
- Mark a remediation as `verified`
- Produce evidence records on its own authority
- Auto-apply changes without an explicit human approval step

## Implementation

- Parse AI output into typed Zod (or equivalent) schemas before use; reject or flag unparseable output.
- Persist provenance: model, timestamp, feature id, and `ai_generated: true` (shown in UI).
- Suggested remediations enter the workflow at `suggested` only.
- Include a confidence field on explanations/suggestions and display it.
- Only deterministic checks (or explicit human decisions) may set `passed` / `failed` / `verified`.
